.TH "CSSNUMERICVALUE.MUL" "3JS" "August 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSNumericValue.mul \- CSSNumericValue: mul() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]mul()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R]
interface multiplies the \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] by the supplied
values.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
mul()
mul(number1)
mul(number1, number2)
mul(number1, number2, /* \&..., */ numberN)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]number1\f[R], \&..., \f[B]numberN\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
Either a number or a \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R].
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]CSSMathProduct\f[R], or a \f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] if
\f[CR]this\f[R] and every argument are plain numbers, or all but one of
them are.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Thrown if an invalid type was passed to the method.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
.IP
.EX
\f[B]let\f[R] mathProduct = CSS.px(23).mul(CSS.percent(4)).mul(CSS.cm(3)).mul(CSS.in(9));
\f[I]// Prints \(dqcalc(23px * 4% * 3cm * 9in)\(dq\f[R]
console.log(mathProduct.toString());
.EE
